experiment: partprobe
  instrument        partprobe   trial seed 000000000135bdde   214 trials per creature
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          `ctxself` refused DNA v52 at p = 0.540 where a
                    SUPERVISED readout of the same population reaches
                    0.740. Is the loss the fixed CUT -- in which case a
                    learned partition recovers it -- or something else?
  the bar           BUILD only if an unsupervised partition reaches
                    p >= 0.65. The effect scales as (2p - 1) and the
                    oracle index buys 65 Hz, so 0.65 keeps ~30% (~20 Hz,
                    detectable at n=9 paired). Below it the mechanism is
                    too small to be a route to naming however significant.
  read-only         no learning, no genome field, nothing shipped.

