    -> THE WINDOW IS NOT THE GAP: the creature's own gate scores
       close to the host's. What separates this from v53's 0.643 is
       the taught setting or the kernel, not the window.

  BUILD THE LATCHED INDEX -- the word is separable in the auditory
  code WITHOUT the labels and WITHOUT restarts, at 1.000 on a single
  pass (1.000 supervised), where the best unsupervised partition of the
  MOTOR state reaches 0.670. That keeps 100% of the conditional effect
  against v52's 8%, or ~65 Hz.

  The mechanism is most of the way built: `active_ctx_` is written only
  when the source is active and HOLDS otherwise, so an index formed
  while the word plays already survives into the reward window. What
  has to change is `ctx_present_`, which gates the cash-in as well as
  the index, so a silent ear at reward time currently sends the update
  to the shared bias instead of the latched context's table.

  Note what this does NOT show: that an unsupervised partition of the
  ear TRACKS THE WORD rather than something correlated with it in this
  protocol. Two vowels differing in loudness or onset would split this
  cleanly too. The build's own control has to be `ctxself`'s
  matched-marginal arm, on the paired test, on a fresh seed family.
